# Frontend Implementation Guide

## Overview
This guide details the API endpoints and data structures for integrating **Partnerships**, **Missions**, and **Achievements** into the frontend application.

## 1. Partnerships Module
Manage and display event or platform sponsors.

### Data Model
```typescript
interface Partnership {
  _id: string;
  name: string;
  logo?: string; // URL
  type: 'Event Sponsor' | 'Platform Sponsor';
  description?: string;
  website?: string; // URL
  createdAt: string;
}
```

### API Endpoints
| Method | Endpoint | Description | Payload |
|:--- |:--- |:--- |:--- |
| `GET` | `/partnerships` | List all partnerships | - |
| `GET` | `/partnerships/:id` | Get single partnership | - |
| `POST` | `/partnerships` | Create partnership | `{ name, type, logo?, website?, description? }` |
| `PATCH` | `/partnerships/:id` | Update partnership | `{ ...partial fields }` |
| `DELETE` | `/partnerships/:id` | Delete partnership | - |

---

## 2. Missions Module
Display available missions and track progress.

### Data Model
```typescript
interface MissionCriteria {
  type: string; // e.g., 'play_games'
  target: number; // e.g., 10
}

interface Mission {
  _id: string;
  title: string;
  description?: string;
  reward: number; // XP or Coins
  criteria: MissionCriteria;
  createdAt: string;
}
```

### API Endpoints
| Method | Endpoint | Description | Payload |
|:--- |:--- |:--- |:--- |
| `GET` | `/mission` | List all missions | - |
| `GET` | `/mission/:id` | Get single mission | - |
| `POST` | `/mission` | Create mission | `{ title, reward, criteria: { type, target }, description? }` |
| `PATCH` | `/mission/:id` | Update mission | `{ ...partial fields }` |
| `DELETE` | `/mission/:id` | Delete mission | - |

---

## 3. Achievements Module
Display unlocked medals and rewards.

### Data Model
```typescript
interface Achievement {
  _id: string;
  name: string;
  description?: string;
  icon: string; // URL to image
  missionsRequired: number;
  createdAt: string;
}
```

### API Endpoints
| Method | Endpoint | Description | Payload |
|:--- |:--- |:--- |:--- |
| `GET` | `/achievements` | List all achievements | - |
| `GET` | `/achievements/:id` | Get single achievement | - |
| `POST` | `/achievements` | Create achievement | `{ name, icon, missionsRequired, description? }` |
| `PATCH` | `/achievements/:id` | Update achievement | `{ ...partial fields }` |
| `DELETE` | `/achievements/:id` | Delete achievement | - |

## Integration Tips

### Partnerships
- **Admin**: Create a form with fields for Name, Type (Dropdown), and URL inputs for Logo/Website.
- **User/Public**: Display a carousel of logos. Link the logo to the `website` URL if present.

### Missions
- **Admin**: Form to define `criteria.type` (e.g., 'Win Match', 'Kill Boss') and `criteria.target` (count).
- **User**: List missions with a progress bar (current / target).

### Achievements
- **Admin**: Upload or provide URL for medal icons. Set the `missionsRequired` threshold.

---

## 4. Player Desktop Application
The desktop client for players to manage their career, matchmaking, and subscriptions.

### File Structure
- **`player/dashboard.html`**: Main single-page application (SPA) view. Contains all sections (Matchmaking, Leagues, etc.) hidden/shown via JS.
- **`player/renderer.js`**: Handles UI logic, navigation state, chart rendering (Chart.js), and IPC communication with the main process.

### Features & Implementation

#### Navigation System
- **Sidebar**:
    - **Primary Tabs**: Play (Collapsible), Match History, My Channel, etc.
    - **Sub-Tabs**: Under "Play" -> Matchmaking, Tournaments, Leagues.
- **Logic**: Uses `showSection(navId, sectionId)` to toggle visibility of `.content-section` divs.
- **Active State**: Highlights current tab with neon green accents (`#00FF00`) and background glow.

#### Visual Style ("Pro Gamer" Aesthetic)
- **Theme**: Dark Mode (`#0a0a0a` backgrounds) with high-contrast text and neon green/purple accents.
- **Effects**:
    - **Glassmorphism**: Translucent card backgrounds.
    - **Neon Glows**: `box-shadow` and `drop-shadow` for interactive elements.
    - **3D Badges**: CSS-only metallic badges for achievements (Gold, Silver, Bronze).

#### Core Modules

**1. Matchmaking**
- **Hero Section**: "Find Match" CTA with skewed button design.
- **Stats Grid**: Dashboard showing Current Rank (e.g., Diamond II), Win Rate, and Hours Played.
- **Performance Chart**: Chart.js integration showing MMR/LP trends over time.

**2. Leagues & Standings**
- **Leaderboard**: Ranked table displaying Player Name, Avatar, Country Flag, Elo, and Win Rate.
- **Filters**: Interactive tabs to filter by Region (World, Africa, Europe, Asia, Americas).
- **Highlights**: Top 3 players get distinct Gold/Silver/Bronze row styling. Current user is pinned/highlighted.

**3. Subscriptions**
- **Plans**: "Rookie" (Free), "Pro" ($9.99), "Legend" ($19.99).
- **UI**: Pricing cards with feature lists. "Pro" plan is visually emphasized (scaled up, "Most Popular" badge).
- **Triggers**: Accessible via the "Upgrade to Pro" button in the sidebar.

**4. Missions & Achievements**
- **Missions**: Tiered cards (Common, Rare, Legendary) with animated progress bars and XP rewards.
- **Achievements**: "Hall of Fame" grid with rarity-based hover effects and 3D badge simulations.

### How to Run
1.  **Install Dependencies**: `npm install`
2.  **Start Application**: `npm start`
3.  **Login**: Use test credentials (or register) to access the dashboard.
